id: @(#)pcihost.tok 1.1 26/10/19
purpose: FCode driver for the PCI host bridge of PCs
copyright: Copyright 2006 Sun Microsystems, Inc.  All Rights Reserved
copyright: Copyright 2026 The OpenBoot x86 port contributors
copyright: Use is subject to license terms.

\ The PC counterpart of the SPARC host bridge drivers (psycho, schizo,
\ dev/sun4v-devices/vpci/vpci.tok).  The probing of the devices behind
\ the bridge is done by the generic PCI bus code (dev/pci/pcibus.fth);
\ this driver supplies the configuration space access (mechanism #1),
\ the address mapping and the address space to assign.
\
\ After loading this driver, the platform calls its "master-probe" method
\ to create the nodes of the PCI devices.

Fcode-Version3

headerless

" pci" name
" pci" device-type
3 encode-int " #address-cells" property
2 encode-int " #size-cells" property
" PNP0A03" encode-string " compatible" property
d# 33.333.333 encode-int " clock-frequency" property

fload ${BP}/dev/pc/pci/common.fth
fload ${BP}/dev/pc/pci/bus-ops.fth
fload ${BP}/dev/pci/pcibus.fth
fload ${BP}/dev/pc/pci/methods.fth
fload ${BP}/dev/pc/pci/resources.fth

init-resources

\ The memory window, as seen from the root node
: make-ranges  ( -- )
   0 0 encode-bytes
   h# 0200.0000 en+  0 en+  pci-mem-base en+	\ PCI memory space
   pci-mem-base en+				\ Processor address
   0 en+  pci-mem-limit pci-mem-base - en+	\ Size
   " ranges" property
;
make-ranges

end0
